 ## Background
-The Single Scattering Propagator is derived from the radiative transfer equation and the path integral formulation of light transport [S1]. It formalizes the concept of light scattering exactly once, separating it from the unscattered (direct) and multiply scattered (indirect) components. This separation is crucial for efficient rendering algorithms, as $G_d$ can be handled by existing direct lighting techniques, while $G_s$ requires specialized methods for participating media [S1]. The formulation corresponds directly to the standard single scattering ray marching algorithm used in computer graphics [S1].
